# Header: the host forwards every FSEvents change under a bind source to
# /proc/ctrs/fsnotify (patch 0006), including the changes this guest made
# itself through virtiofs. An event is skipped only when it provably
# reports the guest's own change: a removed name that is already negative
# here, or a name whose inode this guest changed since a notification last
# named it and whose LOOKUP returns the same node with the cached size,
# mtime and ctime. Any other same-node event refreshes the attributes from
# that reply and is raised in place, keeping the dentry. A Mac edit right
# after the guest's own write is therefore always raised. Kind s (rescan)
# reports that the host lost events: the connection epoch is bumped, and
# on virtiofs a stale-epoch dentry is revalidated with a LOOKUP rather
# than dropped, so mounts on unchanged directories stay attached.
